Original commit body from b6b46d71dd067018e57e25f3ceae7be62c8962ec:

check_partial_linker_requirements looked up a table keyed jni /
swift_objc / dependency with diag.linker_name, which carries the
registered name (jni-linker), so the lookup never hit: no package
suggestion was ever produced and the WI-ruman relevance gate never ran.

LinkerRequirement now declares the languages that can satisfy it
(carried on RequirementStatus); the table is gone, so there is no
second key to drift. 16 linkers declare them. The gate now silences,
e.g., a Tauri app with a Rust frontend ("0 JavaScript/TypeScript
files"). A suggested package that is already installed is dropped.
Label "CGO-LINKER linker" becomes "CGO linker".

LANGUAGE_PACKAGES named the wrong package for 22 of 56 languages
(sql/lua/html/css are in -mainstream, cuda/proto/graphql in -common);
the unanalyzed-files warning used it live. Regenerated (74 entries) and
checked by a test that reads every @register_analyzer in the tree.

